{
 "_provenance": "Vendored from EarthSciModels components/gaschem/pollu.esm (commit eb2a54f), reaction_systems.Pollu without its inline tests. The scaling tier's generator reads this copy so that generation never depends on an EarthSciModels checkout.",
 "reference": {
  "doi": "10.1137/0915076",
  "citation": "Verwer, J. G.: Gauss-Seidel iteration for stiff ODEs from chemical kinetics, SIAM Journal on Scientific Computing, 15(5), 1243-1250, 1994.",
  "url": "https://epubs.siam.org/doi/10.1137/0915076",
  "notes": "Source: GasChem.jl src/Pollu.jl @ 8c12c048482b515fb8eb2110bf8ab4b4f4e71309 (esm-4sxf). Hand-translated from the upstream Catalyst @reaction_network. POLLU is a classic stiff-ODE air-pollution benchmark: 20 species, 25 reactions (15 thermal + 10 photolytic). Reactions are numbered R1..R25 following the canonical POLLU ordering -- the upstream rate-constant names (k2, k3, k6, ...) already encode these indices, and the j-prefixed photolysis constants fill the remaining indices. Every reaction rate is a single rate-constant parameter and every substrate stoichiometry is 1, so the ESM mass-action rate law v = k * prod(S_i) reproduces the upstream ReactionSystem exactly regardless of combinatoric_ratelaws (src/Pollu.jl builds the model with combinatoric_ratelaws=false). The rate constants are the pre-scaled per-second / per-ppb values from src/Pollu.jl (k3 updated to match Fontana pollu.f upstream). Inline-test expected values are an upstream reference run of GasChem.jl Pollu() (Rosenbrock23, abstol=reltol=1e-12); the pollu_benchmark O3 values at 60 s and 3600 s reproduce the published POLLU reference solution to ~1e-8. POLLU's deliberately extreme stiffness (rate constants spanning k23~8e-7 to k19~7e9 1/s) is why this document declares solver.stiffness = \"high\" (esm-spec 2.2): an explicit non-stiff method cannot integrate it -- Julia's Tsit5 gives up with retcode MaxIters on every assertion of every test in this file -- while each binding's implicit pick (scipy BDF, Rosenbrock23) integrates the full 3600 s benchmark in well under a second and reproduces the upstream Rosenbrock23 trajectory. The declaration is what carries that fact to all three bindings; the inline-test gates used to carry a per-file solver table each instead, and no longer do."
 },
